Dear Rachel,

JAGS throws an error when there is a conflict between the model, the data and the inits. Hence, when a chain for N gets initialized at a value that is smaller than any of the counts at that site. To avoid that, provide inits that are equal to the max count for each site and year and to be sure, perhaps add 1 or 2. Then, provide that as inits for the N's.

Best regards  --- Marc

