Marc's right about the error, and here lambda has to be positive, so a Normal(0, 0.1) prior won't work (fwiw, estimating independent U(0, 1) p for every observation is likely to blow up your variance).  If you happen to have missed certain sites during certain years but still want a guess at abundance from these sites, you could move N back into the i/k loop, i.e., N[i, k]~dpois(lambda[i, k]); y[o]~dbin(p[site[o], visit[o], year[o]], N[site[o], year[o]])

