From u72444bb824190d51 at groups.google.com  Tue Apr 23 02:54:30 2019
From: u72444bb824190d51 at groups.google.com (Mike Meredith)
Date: Tue, 23 Apr 2019 02:54:30 +0000
Subject: Changes to 'sample' in R 3.6.0
Message-ID: <djlqnUiuZr4.weWBp_qkDQAJ@hmecology.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/hmecology/c/djlqnUiuZr4/m/weWBp_qkDQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi all,

Just an FYI so y'all aren't baffled when trying to rerun code with new versions of R and finding you have different values in spite of setting the seed.

R version 3.6.0 is due for release on Friday 26 April 2019 and has a new default algorithm for the 'sample' family of functions. This will affect the following AHMbook functions, which will no longer return the same values for a given seed:
Chapter 9 : sim.spatialDS, sim.spatialHDS
Chapter 10 : wigglyOcc
Chapter 21 : simPPe, simDataDK
Chapter 22 : sim.spatialDSline
To recreate the values used in the book, run RNGkind(sample.kind = "Rounding") before setting the seed. That call will throw an error with versions prior to 3.6.0, so if including it in a script use
if(getRversion() >= "3.6.0")
  RNGkind(sample.kind = "Rounding")

This has all arisen because the old ("Rounding") algorithm does not in fact sample uniformly for large numbers, and that needed to be fixed. The new default ("Rejection") is correct, so that's the one to use unless you really need the old one to reproduce previous values.

Regards, Mike

