I've been working with these models in the last week and I've run into another issue I can't seem to get around. I've run simple Poisson and zero-inflated Poisson models with covariates on both detection and abundance and the parameter estimates seem reasonable. However, when I try to add random effects (so far just on site abundance), my derived quantities for yearly abundance explode - they're unreasonably high and have huge SDs. This happens whether I add a trend to the model or keep independence among years. Does anyone have any thoughts on why this could be?

